{
  "regeln": [
    "Maintain the signature painted‑world aesthetic and ensure every visual directly illustrates the narrated business action, event, or figure.",
    "Match pacing to format: rapid conflict beats and visual variety for Shorts; broader narrative arcs for long‑form videos.",
    "Open with a sharp visual hook that states the core commercial conflict and close with a clear resolution beat.",
    "Include a concrete, unexpected turning‑point beat in every script where the story direction shifts.",
    "All narrated facts, dates, figures, and visuals must be verifiable from reliable sources; never substitute vague metaphors for specific business actions.",
    "Synchronize narration, subtitles, and visual changes precisely throughout the video.",
    "Place mandatory spoken calls to like, share, and save at the format‑specific positions; do not replace or relocate them.",
    "Avoid filler imagery: never fill missing content with unrelated stock, background‑only frames, or lifeless documentary photos.",
    "Preserve the established presenters (blue‑eyed man with fedora for Business Origin Stories, black‑haired man with cyan glasses for AI Tools Explained) and re‑introduce them meaningfully throughout the video.",
    "Treat audience dips and reviewer comments as provisional data; test isolated fixes without overgeneralising from a single defect.",
    "Never override source‑supported facts, factual limits, or approved voice styles; prefer concrete observable fixes over unverified retention claims."
  ],
